doc: StoreSVar's per-object number write (gorge effStoreSVar, events.StoreSVar -> Object.RuntimeSVars; CR 400.7): B the value (any ValueRef, evaluated at the write), C the SVar name (Table.SVarNames index, low 4 bits) with the delete-on-default flag (kop.StoreNumDel) and the printed default beside it (kop.StoreNumDefault); the target is the resolving source. The number is a record of the object-set store (kind osNum) keyed by the object, whatever zone it is in: only a departure from the battlefield clears it (gorge's wasBattlefield reset), so a write after the source left persists on the departed object. dirac/act_storenum.go.
